course: dictionary
lesson: 6445
title: Words that share a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A namesake is a person or thing that has the same name as another one. Sometimes a thing is named after a person, so that person is its namesake.
explain: Use the clues in the sentence to find out who or what the namesake is. «The ship was named after the queen, its namesake.» The ship has the queen's name, so the queen is its namesake. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Namesake is a noun, so you can write a namesake or namesakes. Phrases like «his namesake» or «a famous namesake» show you how it is used.
fact: A namesake is a person or thing with the same name as another.
fact: «Namesake» can also mean a person or thing that was named after someone.
fact: In «SpongeBob», Patrick is a sea star, and Squidward is named like a squid.
fact: SpongeBob's namesake is a real sea sponge, which is a simple animal with no brain that filters water.
fact: The plural of namesake is namesakes.
exercise: «The ship was named after the queen, its namesake.» Who is the namesake in this sentence? | *The queen | The ship | The sea | The sailor
exercise: Ella was named after her gran, also called Ella. What is her gran to Ella? | Her holiday | A pet | *Her namesake | A teacher
exercise: Two children in a class are both called Sam. What are they? | *Namesakes | Twins | Best friends | Captains
test: Which real animal is SpongeBob's namesake? | *A sea sponge | An octopus | A sea star | A squid
test: «The town was named after its founder, so the founder is its namesake.» What is a namesake? | A small animal that lives in the sea | A type of weather | *A person or thing named after someone | A rival
exam: Which sentence uses namesake correctly? | The namesake was wet and cold | Namesake is a colour of paint | Ruby ate her namesake for lunch | *Ruby and her gran are both called Ruby, so they are namesakes
